{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>My soul.</b> The meaning of נפשי is \"my soul,\" [namely] that I desired You in the night." "<b>Also my spirit within me, I seek You early.</b> Now man has both nefesh and ruach, as I explained in Ecclesiastes (Ecclesiastes 3:21)." "<b>For when.</b> [When] they see Your judgments in the earth, they will learn righteousness." "<b>Inhabitants of the world.</b> The name of the place of habitation."], :book :isaiah, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Isaiah, by M. Friedlander; Society of Hebrew Literature, London 1877" "https://www.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH001338443"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:55:13.069684472Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}